Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Description: Backported and Experimental Type Hints for Python 3.9+
 typing_extensions complements the standard-library typing module by
 providing runtime support for type hints that are only available in
 newer Python versions, and experimental type-system features proposed
 in draft PEPs before they are accepted into typing.
 .
 This package is fetched under the VitexSoftware Vitexus fork so it can
 be pinned to a specific upstream release tag (4.16.0), which several
 other packages (notably python3-anyio) depend on for the PEP 661
 `sentinel` API.
